---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Mermaid from '../components/Mermaid.astro';
---
<Base title="Engineering lab — Khaled Tlili"><div class="eyebrow">05 / Engineering lab</div><h1>Explore systems<span class="accent">.</span></h1><section class="section"><h2>Interactive architecture diagrams</h2><Mermaid/></section><section class="section"><h2>Design patterns explorer</h2>{[['Strategy','Encapsulate interchangeable algorithms behind an interface. Example: pricing strategies.'],['Factory','Centralize creation logic when construction depends on a configuration or invariant.'],['Adapter','Translate an external interface into the interface your application expects.'],['Decorator','Wrap an implementation to add behavior without changing its contract.']].map(([name,desc])=><details><summary>{name}</summary><p>{desc}</p></details>)}</section><section class="section"><h2>PHP examples playground</h2><p>Adjust the input to explore a PHP expression. Results are simulated in JavaScript; no arbitrary PHP execution.</p><pre><code>function double(int $n): int &#123; return $n * 2; &#125;</code></pre><label for="number">Integer input</label><input id="number" type="number" min="-1000000" max="1000000" step="1" value="5"/><p>Result: <output id="result">10</output></p></section><section class="section"><h2>System design case studies</h2><details><summary>Reliable asynchronous order processing</summary><p>Use an outbox to atomically store events alongside changes; consumers handle duplicate delivery with idempotency keys. Trade-off: eventual consistency and operational complexity.</p></details><details><summary>Read-heavy catalog service</summary><p>Use cache-aside with TTL and request coalescing. Measure hit rate and stale reads; keep the database authoritative. Trade-off: freshness versus latency.</p></details></section></Base><script>const number=document.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('#number')!;number.addEventListener('input',()=>{const n=number.valueAsNumber;document.querySelector('#result')!.textContent=Number.isSafeInteger(n)&&Math.abs(n)<=1000000?String(n*2):'Enter a valid integer'});</script>